============================================================================================
PART 4 -- diagnostic, the Lipschitz tail, and the rho bridge
============================================================================================
  exact census floor (primitive, maxP <= 18): |G'| = 7/858 = 0.008159 at (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13)
  adversarial-family min: 0.023148 ({1..11, 26})
  hill-descent min:       0.008159 at [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13]
  OVERALL MIN OBSERVED:   0.008159

  VERDICT: FLOOR SIGNAL -- none of the explicitly listed finite probes moved
  below the bounded census minimum; no convergence claim follows from this sample.

  PROVED (unconditional Lipschitz tail): |G'_P| >= 2(M(P)-1/14)/maxP >= 1/(91*maxP)
  PROVED (the rho bridge, one line):     rho = v*/maxP = r_P/(pi|G'|maxP) <= 12/(pi|G'_P|)
  => on every stratum where |G'| >= gamma:  rho <= 12/(pi*gamma); with gamma = census
     floor 0.00816: rho <= 468.2 (uniform, that stratum).
